  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Keep about half of answers as regular -s plurals and half as regular -es plurals.",
      "Never make the answer an irregular plural, an -ies change, or an f/fe change. Never target baby, city, family, puppy, party, story, leaf, wolf, fish, sheep, child, man, woman, person, foot, or tooth.",
      "Never put the correct plural in the stem. Name the singular, or write a short kid sentence with two of these.",
      "Do not describe a picture in the stem. Add media with the singular lemma only.",
      "Choices are whole lowercase words only. No letters, no IPA, no possessives with 's.",
      "Tier 1 distractors are the singular plus two silly wrong endings. Tier 2 swaps -s and -es. Tier 3 uses near-miss spellings, especially on words that already end in s, x, ch, or sh.",
      "Kid world only: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands. Use <NAME> for any person."
    ]
  },
